But they have no roots. Therefore, they do not last long. As soon as they face hardship or persecution because of the message, they quickly turn away from the faith.
While others received the seed that fell on rocks. They are the ones who hear the message. But then, the worries of the world and the illusory gains intervene to obscure it. Preventing it from producing.
But others received the seed that fell on good ground. They are the ones who hear the message and understand it. They produce a crop, a hundred, sixty, or thirty times what the farmer planted. The story is about the weeds.
Jesus said to a crowd, "This is how the Kingdom of Heaven is. He told them another parable and said, 'A man planted good seed in a field.'
While everyone was sleeping, his enemy came. The enemy sowed weeds among the wheat and then left.
